@verbs configuration config settings
@tier player
@title configuration: everything you can adjust, in one place
@see columns inform earmuffs editor wimpy speak consent

  configuration
  configuration <category>
  configuration <category> <topic>
  configuration <category> <topic> <value>

It gathers what many other commands change one by one. With nothing,
it shows it all; with a category, just that one; with a topic, its
value and what it takes; and with a value, it changes it. A value that
does not do is refused, naming the ones that would.

The categories are:

  terminal          the terminal type, columns and rows
  information       whether the game describes everything in detail,
                    and which notices you want to receive
  communication     earmuffs and what they block, the editor, the
                    point of view and the prompt
  character         the combat mode, wimpy and the language you speak
  consents          what you let others do with you

The first three belong to your account and are the same for all your
characters; the last two belong to each character. Next to each topic,
between brackets, is the command that does the same, with its own help.
